  "question": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{MgSO}_4$ on reaction with $\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH}$ and $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{HPO}_4$ forms a white crystalline precipitate. What is its formula?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BJQtm",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Mg}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_4\\right) \\mathrm{PO}_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ngVhq",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{Mg}_3\\left(\\mathrm{PO}_4\\right)_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HHrYY",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{MgCl}_2 \\cdot \\mathrm{MgSO}_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PD1N0",
      "text": "\n$\\mathrm{MgSO}_4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{MgSO}_4$ on reaction with $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{HPO}_4$ (disodium hydrogen phosphate) in presence of $\\mathrm{NH}_4 \\mathrm{OH}$ to give white precipitate of magnesium ammonium phosphate $\\left(\\mathrm{Mg}\\left(\\mathrm{NH}_4\\right) \\mathrm{PO}_4\\right)$.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/MpRey9k-Y2s158WLfD5sHyIYsJf5OFY_P-DHgLZbHkM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
